  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through next Monday)\nIssued at 154 PM CDT Tue Oct 13 2026\n\nOnce the upper trough moves out of our area and the cold front\nfully pushes through, a stable airmass and cooler temperatures\nwill be left in its wake for the rest of the week. Highs may \nstart in the 70s and 60s on Thursday, but by Friday we may not \neven escape the 50s during the day time. This weekend, below \naverage high temperatures will continue in the 60s and 70s. The \nlatest 13Z NBM has introduce more freezing (<32F) temperatures \nacross our northern zones Saturday morning, while the rest of the \nCWA could range in the mid to upper 30s. Rain chances through the \nextended period remain absent due to high pressure aloft.\n\nRangel",
